CLFiler
=======
Improved Filer-like application.


Multiple windows with copy/move and Drag-drop files/directories between.
When you drop the files(s) then you will asked to Copy or Move the files.

Disk Treeview at the left side.
Archives and applications will be added to treeview only when opened and will be removed when
the parent (or root) directory is selected because treeview content is refreshed and rescanned again
to keep in sync with the actual filesystem (for cases when a directory removed or renamed by another application),

CLFiler can detect following filing sytems at start:
ADFS, SCSIFS, CDFS, IDEFS, RAM, SDFS, SATAFS, DOSFS, FAT32FS, ShareFS

You may add manually some not detected filesystems (FS) or root directories in the
"!Boot.Choices.CLFiler.predefined-roots" text file. Any entries in that file will be added to the drive selector list.
This is a workaround for not automatically detected file systems.
Note: the checking is filesystems actually exists is not performed to avoid situations when many filesystem icons 
appeared on the iconbar. The syntax for text file "predefined-roots" is simple. 
Write every root path, like you see it in the legacy RISC OS lFiler, in a new line, like this:
 Fat32fs::SSD_FAT
 NFS::Ti_FAT
 Lanman98::Ti_FAT

Keyboard shortcuts
==================
Up/Down
Left/Right   - Move selection bar in the current directory
Return       - Open or run selected directory or file
Del / Ctrl-K - Delete select file(s)
Ctrl-A       - Select all in the current directory
Ctrl-Z       - Clear selection (deselect all)
Ctrl-C       - "copy" file(s) to internal clipboard to "paste" into other directory
Shift-C      - "Copy As" copy first selected file with new name in the same directory
Ctrl-X       - "cut" file(s) to internal clipboard to "paste" into other directory
Ctrl-V       - "paste" (copy) the file(s) that was "copied" or "cut" before.
Ctrl-D       - Create new directory
Ctrl-F       - Toggle "Search" mode.
Ctrl-H       - Open parent directory
Ctrl-N       - Open new window
Ctrl-M	     - Open new window with all toolbars off.
Ctrl-R       - Rename file
Ctrl-S       - Set file type
Ctrl-O       - Stamp files (set current timestamp as edit date)
Ctrl-T       - toggle top toolbar
Shift-T      - toggle left side tree view
Ctrl-W       - set current directory
Ctrl-Up      - go up level (to parent directory)
Ctrl-Left    - go backward (to previous directory)
Ctrl-Right   - go forward  (reverse go backward)
F1           - Help
F2           - Set "Large icons" view mode
F3           - Set "Small icons" view mode
F4           - Set "Full info" view mode
F11          - Refresh current directory



